PS5 HFR1 / CS2 Nuke / AMD L3 CAT Steam WebHelper A/B/A
2026-11-07. Original CS2, -insecure local Nuke replay at 1x, first-person,
seek 10048 (~02:38), fresh server resume tick 12178 all phases. 10s warm-up,
reseeking and 15s scored. System RADV 26.0.8, MP1 off, X11 1080p240 Flip,
per-process game settings restored byte-for-byte. FPS and tail metrics are
shown-frame Present UST cadence. All three windows used Flip throughout.

A1/A2 had full ffff masks for Steam WebHelper, B f/000f on both domains.
Hardware and sysfs confirmed two 4 MiB domains with 16 ways, B allowed 4 ways
or 1 MiB of new allocations per domain for WebHelper. The default group was
ffff/ffff throughout. The game ran in that group with no CPU mask restriction.
The experiment group had no assigned CPUs. MB settings were unchanged.
A shared CAT group changes allocation for its members; it does not create a
private or larger L3. All 154 observed helper threads were assigned at each
boundary. CS2 and other desktop tasks were left outside that group. Discord
was not running in the measured windows. Steam WebHelper was mostly idle.

A1 had two distinct Flip serials with identical UST and MSC. The scorer counts
one unique completion instant for such a tie, identically across all phases.
The controller re-established the full-mask group after A1 before B, and
recorded the applied mask and task membership in each phase. At the end it
removed the experiment group, unmounted resctrl, and stopped the fallback timer.
No new matching machine-check/MSR/GPU/OOM events were seen; CS2 closed normally.

B displayed about 2 FPS more than the mean of the controls in this sequence.
B's 1% low and P99 essentially match A2. This single restricted run does not
establish a repeatable improvement in average FPS or under heavier background load.
Linux documentation: https://docs.kernel.org/filesystems/resctrl.html

